{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792336005,"nonce":"e6dVZcbX/qFdArze3/tZKPWR5KU=","title":"Keymaps of popular editors","message":"The user asked that RayDE be able to adopt the key bindings of popular IDEs.\n\nBuilt (4f31a8a, part of the Settings page, 72bb840): Visual Studio Code (the default), IntelliJ IDEA, Sublime Text, Eclipse, Visual Studio (Windows and Linux) and Xcode (Mac), each with its Mac and Windows/Linux keys for the commands RayDE has. Chosen from a tile on the Key bindings page or Select Keymap in the command center, kept in the keymap section of .rayde/settings.json; the user's own changes in .rayde/keybindings.json stay on top. The terminal gives the workbench the keys of its toggles, quick open, the palette and settings whichever keymap is chosen.\n\nNot done: Vim (modal editing, which belongs in the editor and needs ashui's CodeEditor) and Emacs (its keys are chord sequences); chord sequences for any keymap (Sublime's and VS Code's Cmd+K Cmd+S, IntelliJ's Double Shift); importing a VS Code keybindings.json or an IntelliJ keymap file; keymaps for commands RayDE does not have yet, as it gets them; keys that depend on the keyboard layout.","files":null}]}